    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="16" spacingafter="2" fontweight="bold">D2 I-95 PEDESTRIAN BRIDGE</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">C014 - End Bent 1 Backwall, Cheek Walls and Tie-Back Straps</paragraph>
    <section name="WorkingNotes" capture="False" hide="true">
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#43505C">Working notes (hidden; not part of the submitted calculation): how this edition was produced, its tool status and the open bookkeeping items.</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Blockpad edition of End_Bent_Backwall_Design.ipynb (calculation package 4f877bd2c240; case SHA-256 0ff135b29eacfd445c6c4a9983cf1e6c471c17fee747e0aab41f357bacd235d2). Same inputs, equations and load combinations as the notebook; every result below was recomputed and compared with the notebook. Blockpad edition written by scripts/build_backwall_bpad.py from the same case; every definition was evaluated independently and compared with the notebook to 1 part in 10⁹.</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Status: adopted CAD geometry reconciled 19 October 2026 (D-053 backwall tops, D-055 model; D-049 analysis export); single centered #4 cheek mat at 10 in each way. Prerequisites remain pending (Section 12).</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Pending before final design: geotechnical confirmation of 2 in maximum settlement above the cap bottom (SDG 3.13.2.N.3); strap elevation at an MSE reinforcement level; beam shrinkage strain; environment for the covers; matching current bearing-load analyses; cheek mat development and cap/lug load path. Geometry, journal Kz and landing basis are reconciled. The pile-head force V_pile is not in the FBMP model; raise the strap toward e_res or confirm the piles carry it.</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">A ✓ status covers only the recomputed numerical checks; it is not design acceptance. Recalculate in Blockpad after any input change.</paragraph>
    </section>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Project: D2 I-95 Pedestrian Bridge · common end-bent design.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Codes: AASHTO LRFD Bridge Design Specifications, 10th edition (2024); FDOT Structures Design Guidelines (SDG) and Structures Detailing Manual (SDM), January 2026.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Inputs are highlighted amber; results are the green tables.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True">1. Design basis</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Tie-back straps in the backwall extend into the MSE fill and resist the end-bent horizontal load and overturning. Attachment requires total settlement of the soil above the cap bottom of 2 in or less (SDG 3.13.2.N.3).</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• The single pile row is effectively pinned (FBMP fixity 0.10), so moments are taken about the pile top O. The strap force is F = max(H, M / y_strap); the piles supply M / y_strap − H at O.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Vertical-load arms are measured from the pile line shifted 3 in toward the fill (placement tolerance, SDG 3.13.2.N.3). Permanent loads take the maximum factor on an overturning arm and the minimum on a stabilizing arm; live load and wind uplift take no stabilizing credit.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Pedestrian load only: 90 psf live-load surcharge. Backfill φ = 30°, δ = 0, γ = 115 pcf, active Coulomb pressure.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• The landing slab bears on the backwall: 50 % of its load goes to gravity design with no stabilizing credit; its weight on the fill acts as an earth surcharge ES.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• The cheek walls retain no fill: wind only. The backwall is designed at the crown height with the strap 1.5 ft above the cap top.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Backwall states: strap slack, soil causes fill-face tension; strap engaged, the strap pull causes span-face tension. Both are designed.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True">2. Inputs</paragraph>
